{"name":"Tavern Taupe","hex":"#9e938f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tavern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A restaurant or bar.","A building containing a bar licensed to sell alcoholic drinks, and offering sleeping accommodations for travelers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tavern"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tavern","blocks":[{"text":"A tavern is a type of business where people gather to drink alcoholic beverages and be served food, such as different types of roast meats and cheese, and where travelers would receive lodging. An inn is a tavern that has a licence to put up guests as lodgers. The word derives from the Latin taberna whose original meaning was a shed, workshop, stall, or pub."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg/330px-Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavern"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg/500px-Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg/500px-Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_a